73
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:26,032
It was working at one point.

74
00:04:26,032 --> 00:04:30,336
But Neuroblox is
constantly evolving.

75
00:04:30,336 --> 00:04:33,573
And so what I wanted to
do with you actually,

76
00:04:33,573 --> 00:04:36,576
is a very simple example.

77
00:04:36,576 --> 00:04:40,847
And that is called the harmonic
oscillator neural mass model.

78
00:04:40,847 --> 00:04:43,283
This is sort of a toy
neural math model.

79
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:47,086
There are some works that
use the harmonic oscillator.

80
00:04:47,086 --> 00:04:51,391
But I think actually it's a very
good example for just testing

81
00:04:51,391 --> 00:04:55,461
out your intuition,
because it's almost

82
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:56,596
like a harmonic oscillator.

83
00:04:56,596 --> 00:04:59,532
But it's kind of a nonlinear
harmonic oscillator.

84
00:04:59,532 --> 00:05:00,733
And you have to--

85
00:05:00,733 --> 00:05:05,338
the challenge is to
get this to oscillate.

86
00:05:05,338 --> 00:05:08,374
If you know
differential equations,

87
00:05:08,374 --> 00:05:15,281
you can actually see that
there's a dxdt is equal to y,

88
00:05:15,281 --> 00:05:20,186
and then dydt is minus omega
squared times x, omega squared

89
00:05:20,186 --> 00:05:24,123
times x, which means that
if you take the derivative

90
00:05:24,123 --> 00:05:26,225
and plug it in, then you
get essentially a harmonic

91
00:05:26,225 --> 00:05:28,494
oscillator, like
differential equation, where

92
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:33,199
the solution of that would be a
sine or cosine with a frequency

93
00:05:33,199 --> 00:05:34,500
omega.

94
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,868
But then you have other terms.

95
00:05:35,868 --> 00:05:39,405
You have essentially
a damping term.

96
00:05:39,405 --> 00:05:42,842
So this thing alone would be a
damped oscillator would never

97
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:45,311
actually oscillate properly.

98
00:05:45,311 --> 00:05:52,018
But then you have a connection
which is A10 of the junction.

99
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:54,821
And the junction could be then
the input of something else.

100
00:05:54,821 --> 00:05:57,323
So in order to get
this oscillate,

101
00:05:57,323 --> 00:06:00,059
you have to actually have two
of the harmonic oscillators

102
00:06:00,059 --> 00:06:01,894
interacting with each other.

103
00:06:01,894 --> 00:06:05,331
So there could be a self
interaction and a interaction

104
00:06:05,331 --> 00:06:06,699
between the oscillators.

105
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:09,135
And I will show you how
to construct this system

106
00:06:09,135 --> 00:06:12,405
and how to get them to behave.

107
00:06:12,405 --> 00:06:15,942
And so the challenge
for you maybe

108
00:06:15,942 --> 00:06:18,644
as an intellectual
challenge, how do we

109
00:06:18,644 --> 00:06:21,347
change the frequency of
these harmonic oscillators?

110
00:06:21,347 --> 00:06:24,684
That would be a little test.

111
00:06:24,684 --> 00:06:26,919
And then the next step
that we want to do

112
00:06:26,919 --> 00:06:30,022
is we want to build
a cortical region.

113
00:06:30,022 --> 00:06:32,358
And we are not going to
do this hierarchically,

114
00:06:32,358 --> 00:06:34,160
not like in the tutorial.

115
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:36,095
But what I wanted to do--

116
00:06:36,095 --> 00:06:38,264
what I want you to do
is to essentially build

117
00:06:38,264 --> 00:06:41,267
a cortical region where
you specify essentially

118
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:44,837
how many winner takes
all circuits you use

119
00:06:44,837 --> 00:06:48,374
and then build it
and simulate it.

120
00:06:48,374 --> 00:06:52,245
And this is what the
ultimate goal will be.

121
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,946
You will have two
cortical regions

122
00:06:53,946 --> 00:06:58,151
that are combined to each other
or connected to each other.

123
00:06:58,151 --> 00:07:01,554
And you will be able to
see the adjacency matrix

124
00:07:01,554 --> 00:07:03,156
of that coupling.

125
00:07:03,156 --> 00:07:06,125
So this over here
essentially means

126
00:07:06,125 --> 00:07:09,562
the lower half is
C1, where you see

127
00:07:09,562 --> 00:07:11,297
all the connections
between neurons

128
00:07:11,297 --> 00:07:13,166
within a cortical region.

129
00:07:13,166 --> 00:07:16,569
Then you will see
on the top right you

130
00:07:16,569 --> 00:07:19,405
see all the connections of C2.

131
00:07:19,405 --> 00:07:22,275
And then in yellow are
all the connections

132
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:28,114
between the cortical regions.

133
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,082
And this is the flat brain GUI.

