202
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:31,490
Now, just one of the
details about Julia.

203
00:11:31,490 --> 00:11:36,162
Julia is just-in-time
compiled language,

204
00:11:36,162 --> 00:11:40,199
which means that whenever you
execute something in Julia,

205
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:45,504
it compiles at that time, which
means that because this is also

206
00:11:45,504 --> 00:11:49,208
running in the cloud, it will
take a little while until all

207
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:52,011
the differential equation
or JL packages are compiled.

208
00:11:52,011 --> 00:11:54,246
So next time you do
this, it's much faster.

209
00:11:57,116 --> 00:11:58,884
So it will take a while.

210
00:11:58,884 --> 00:12:03,289
So by the way, one of
the interesting details

211
00:12:03,289 --> 00:12:06,125
about this GUI is that, and
this is why we didn't even

212
00:12:06,125 --> 00:12:09,261
